do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 0.001
caption: Onto its surface

@stop into-crust
do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 1e-12
through: yes
caption: Into the crust: nuclei a picometre apart in a lattice, electrons racing between them

@stop neutron-choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop neutron-to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Inward: an atom is almost all empty space

@stop neutron-round-nucleus
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 24
seconds: 5
caption: Its nucleus: protons and neutrons bound by the strong force

@stop neutron-choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: A proton

@stop neutron-to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.35
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a single proton

@stop neutron-round-proton
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 20
seconds: 4
caption: Three quarks in a storm of gluons

@stop neutron-choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: A quark

@stop neutron-to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.35
until-km: 6e-19
caption: One quark

@stop neutron-at-quark
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 4
caption: The smallest thing we know

@stop neutron-let-go
do: pick
target: none
caption: And back out

@stop out-of-crust
do: zoom
rate: -0.7
until-km: 1e-9
caption: Back out through the crust

@stop off-neutron
do: zoom
rate: -0.7
until-km: 1e4
caption: Off the neutron star

@stop out-of-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: -0.6
until-km: 3e18
caption: Out of the galaxy, its hundred billion stars one spiral of light

@stop to-web
do: zoom
rate: -0.45
until-km: 5e21
caption: Out to the cosmic web, galaxies by the million

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 4
seconds: 10
caption: The same universe at every scale, from the cosmic web to a quark. {seen}
